- [Zwingli1526](https://www.uecf.net/books/zwingli-and-bullinger/chapter5.html), Second/Third Articles: supports the analogy and ascension constraint. “May” in the intermediate appropriately avoids proving a figurative interpretation from analogy alone.
- [Marburg Articles](https://germanhistorydocs.org/en/from-the-reformations-to-the-thirty-years-war-1500-1648/ghdi:document-4311),15: shared spiritual reception is not consensus on bodily presence; conscience-qualified love is not modern toleration.
